"""Small source-fidelity guidance delta; no keyword rewriting or automatic truth claim."""
SEMANTIC_PRECISION_GUIDANCE = """
Source precision after bilingual rewriting (apply in generation, compression and review):
1. Role and action status. Leading a bounded task does not establish a formal job title or leadership of the whole project. A defect being confirmed does not mean it was fixed. A named person's responsibility for approval does not establish a completed approval or the applicant's participation in it. A review classification does not establish that the applicant resolved or clarified the item. Preserve explicit leadership, completed actions and formal titles when the source actually establishes them; never use a verb blacklist. When the source merely lacks the stronger action/status, report missing support rather than inventing an opposite fact.
2. Ability and entity identity. Reading documentation or articles establishes that reading activity, not native language, fluency, professional working proficiency or an unsupplied skill grade. Prefer the supported activity or demonstrated deliverable; retain an explicit source-supported grade if provided. Use a supplied official/confirmed organization name. Otherwise preserve the original name and, if useful, an explicitly descriptive translation; do not guess a transliteration or silently change the entity. Mixed-script proper names are allowed. Translate a role or degree separately from the organization name so uncertainty in the name does not erase supported credentials.
3. Events, counted units and ownership. Translate dates by the event they refer to: a repair request/report date is not a repair-work or completion date. Preserve the counted object and denominator, such as assertions versus scripts, and distinguish the test/production environment. Observations from different participant groups do not establish causal improvement; retain group sizes, sample identity and trial status. Supported arithmetic may be shown with its basis, but must not add causation. Preserve the named handoff/maintenance owner when its omission would make past delivery look like the applicant's ongoing responsibility. Whole low-relevance details may be omitted safely; do not treat every omitted handoff sentence as an error. Supported team improvements may remain with the applicant's actual contribution.
Review against original evidence independently for each language, including entry headings and summaries, not just bullets or keywords. Use the existing supported/contradicted/missing_support/ambiguous judgments and separate material omissions. Distinguish an actual contradiction from unsupported strengthening, grammar ambiguity and a useful but safely omitted detail. A fluent rewrite must not create a new method, purpose, role, capability or outcome. These instructions do not themselves establish model improvement or render acceptance.
"""
